    "id": "igr7D8pIB2c7"
   },
   "source": [
    "In general, compressing the image to 60-80% percent of its original size lowers its quality but human eye won't be even able to notice it. Therefore, we can win in storage while keeping almost the same image quality. Find out the range of  k 's which result in keeping only 60-80% of the size of the original image. For what  k 's there is no reason to use SVD for the sake of reducing storage space?\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "The number of scalars stored by a rank-k SVD approximation of an $m \\times n$ image (per channel) is\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\text{size}(k) \\;=\\; k\\,(m + n + 1),$$\n",
    "\n",
    "while the raw image takes $m \\cdot n$ values per channel.  Solving $k(m+n+1) = \\alpha\\, m n$ for $\\alpha = 0.6$ and $\\alpha = 0.8$ gives the band reported above by the cell: every k in $[\\texttt{lower\\_bound\\_k},\\; \\texttt{upper\\_bound\\_k}]$ stores 60–80 % of the original data, which empirically still looks essentially indistinguishable from the original to a human eye.\n",
    "\n",
    "The break-even point is\n",
    "\n",
    "$$k^{*} \\;=\\; \\frac{m n}{m + n + 1}.$$\n",
    "\n",
    "For any $k > k^{*}$ (printed as compression_limit), the SVD representation is larger than the raw pixel matrix, so using SVD for the sake of saving storage no longer makes sense - at that point you are paying extra memory for no gain in visual.  In practice the useful regime is $k \\ll k^{*}$, where the dominant singular values capture the bulk of the image energy and the trailing ones (which mostly encode noise / fine texture) can be safely discarded.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 101,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "9iEVa6t6ykkQ"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def compressed_size(k, image):\n",
    "    if image.ndim == 3:\n",
    "        m, n, c = image.shape\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        m, n = image.shape\n",
    "        c = 1\n",
    "    size_comp = c * k * (m + n + 1)\n",
    "    return size_comp\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 102,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "7MiFQeN2bKS3"
   },
   "outputs": [
